 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nBigQuery identifier case sensitivity not preserved in table references\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing BigQuery SQL with table identifiers that contain mixed case, the case is not being preserved correctly. This affects table references where the original casing should be maintained.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot.dialects import BigQuery\n\n# Parse a simple query with mixed case table name\nsql = \"SELECT * FROM MyTable\"\nparsed = sqlglot.parse_one(sql, dialect=BigQuery)\nprint(parsed.sql(dialect=BigQuery))\n\n# Expected: SELECT * FROM MyTable  \n# Actual: SELECT * FROM mytable\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when BigQuery dialect processes table identifiers - the case is being converted to lowercase even when it should be preserved according to BigQuery's case sensitivity rules.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nTable identifiers should maintain their original case when generating SQL output, especially for BigQuery dialect where case sensitivity matters for table references.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nTable identifiers are being converted to lowercase, which can cause issues when the original SQL relied on specific casing for table names.\n</issue>\n",
